11 3 Definitions.
12 I. Inthisact:
13 (a) "Applicable codes" means the New Hampshire state building code and any local
14 technical amendments, excluding fire prevention and fire safety codes except as referenced by the
15 statebuildingcode.
16 (b) "Approved agency" means an individual or entity that is authorized as permitted by
17 this section to perform building code inspection services and construction document reviews as an
18 alternative to those conducted by local government agencies. Private providers may include
19 professionalssuchasengineers,architects,orICC-certifiedbuildingofficials.
20 (c) "Audit" means the process to assess that construction document review and
21 inspectionserviceshavegenerallybeenperformedproperlybytheprivateprovider.
22 (d) "Approved agency services" means the review of construction documents and
23 inspection services to determine compliance with applicable codes, each as required by the state
24 buildingcode.
25 (e) "Construction documents" means written, graphic, and pictorial documents prepared
26 or assembled for describing the design, location, and physical characteristics of the elements of a
27 project necessary for obtaining a building permit. Construction documents do not include
28 applicationsordocumentsgeneratedforzoningorplanningapprovals.
29 (f) "Building inspection" means the inspection of an improvement to land as required by
30 the state building code as part of a project to develop or improve an improvement to the land,
31 building,orstructure.
